{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-001", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "I ___ a junior high school student.", "choices": ["am", "is", "are", "be"], "answer": "am", "explanation": "主語が I のときは am です。be動詞は主語によって形が変わります。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-002", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "My father ___ a doctor.", "choices": ["is", "am", "are", "be"], "answer": "is", "explanation": "My father は 1 人（三人称単数）なので is です。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-003", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "You ___ very kind.", "choices": ["are", "am", "is", "be"], "answer": "are", "explanation": "You は 1 人でも複数でも are を使います。日本語の「あなた」につられて is にしないよう注意します。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-004", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "Tom and I ___ good friends.", "choices": ["are", "am", "is", "be"], "answer": "are", "explanation": "「A と B」で 2 人以上なので are です。I が入っていても am にはなりません。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-005", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "These books ___ very interesting.", "choices": ["are", "is", "am", "be"], "answer": "are", "explanation": "These books は複数です。主語が単数か複数かで is / are を選びます。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-006", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "It ___ cold today.", "choices": ["is", "are", "am", "be"], "answer": "is", "explanation": "天気を言うときの主語は it です。it は単数なので is を使います。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-007", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "My sister and her friend ___ in the library.", "choices": ["are", "is", "am", "be"], "answer": "are", "explanation": "主語が 2 人なので are です。直前の friend が単数でも、主語全体を見て決めます。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "be-pres-008", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "I ___ from Osaka.", "choices": ["am", "is", "are", "do"], "answer": "am", "explanation": "「〜出身です」は be動詞で表します。日本語の「です」に do は使いません。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "be-pres-009", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "わたしは学生です。", "blocks": ["I", "am", "a", "student"], "answers": [["I", "am", "a", "student"]], "explanation": "英語では「だれが→です→何」の順です。a を落としやすいので気をつけます。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "be-pres-010", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "彼女はわたしの姉です。", "blocks": ["She", "is", "my", "sister"], "answers": [["She", "is", "my", "sister"]], "explanation": "日本語の「姉」「妹」はどちらも sister です。年上か年下かは英語では区別しません。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "be-pres-011", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "その本はおもしろいです。", "blocks": ["The", "book", "is", "interesting"], "answers": [["The", "book", "is", "interesting"]], "explanation": "「おもしろいです」は形容詞なので、be動詞のあとにそのまま置きます。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "be-pres-012", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.be_present", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "わたしたちは同じクラスです。", "blocks": ["We", "are", "in", "the", "same", "class"], "answers": [["We", "are", "in", "the", "same", "class"]], "explanation": "「同じクラスです」は in を使って「同じクラスの中にいる」と表します。"}}
